WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.680
Jie was the last ruler of the Xia dynasty.

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:09.158
He lived in a splendid palace, in great luxury.

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:14.764
Jie held banquets every day and paid no attention to state affairs.

00:00:15.114 --> 00:00:18.978
Mo Xi is a famous figure linked to King Jie.

00:00:19.328 --> 00:00:24.320
The people lived in hardship, but Jie paid no heed to their suffering.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:29.614
Later accounts often describe Jie's loss of virtue in vivid detail.

00:00:29.964 --> 00:00:34.644
However, many of these stories come from later legends.

00:00:34.994 --> 00:00:39.458
When we read history, we must distinguish facts from legend.

00:00:39.808 --> 00:00:45.112
Jie slowly lost the hearts of the people, and the lords turned away from him.

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:50.190
Tang of Shang won support and resolved to rise against Jie.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:54.356
In the end, the Xia dynasty fell to ruin in Jie's hands.

00:00:54.706 --> 00:01:00.346
This story reminds us that power must come with responsibility and virtue.

